---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="How Naturally Restful earns money, and the firewall between commerce and content."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
    <p class="lead">Plain-English version of a legally required notice. Last updated: September 2026.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        <strong>Naturally Restful is reader-supported.</strong> When you buy through certain links
        on this site, the seller pays us a commission. It costs you nothing extra — the price is
        the same whether you use our link or not.
      </p>

      <h2>Which links pay us</h2>
      <p>
        Links that go through our <code>/go/</code> redirect system (for example,
        <code>naturallyrestful.xyz/go/magnesium-glycinate</code>) are affiliate links. They are
        marked <code>rel="nofollow sponsored"</code> in the site code, disclosed near the link,
        and disclosed again on the pages containing them.
      </p>

      <h2>The firewall</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We choose products first, on merit; affiliate programs are checked second. If the best product has no affiliate program, it still gets recommended.</li>
        <li>Commission rates never influence rankings. Where rates differ, that fact is treated as irrelevant to editorial decisions.</li>
        <li>No brand pays to appear on this site or to be named "top pick." There are no sponsored posts. If that ever changes, posts will be labeled unmistakably.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Other income, when it exists</h2>
      <p>
        This site may later carry display advertising and sell its own digital products
        (e.g., guides). Both will be visually distinct from editorial content. Pages whose main
        purpose is a product recommendation carry no display ads.
      </p>

      <h2>What this means for you</h2>
      <p>
        Assume we might earn a commission on anything we link — then judge our recommendations on
        their evidence, which we show our work for. That's the deal, stated plainly, per the
        US FTC's endorsement guides and equivalent UK/EU consumer rules.
      </p>

      <p>Questions? <a href="/contact">Contact us</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
